within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C07A_BetaBlockingAgents.C07AG02_Carvedilol;
model Carvedilol "Carvedilol — default model: Carvedilol_Nikolic2013_reference"
  extends Carvedilol_Nikolic2013_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of carvedilol: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C07A_BetaBlockingAgents.C07AG02_Carvedilol.Carvedilol_Nikolic2013_reference\">Carvedilol_Nikolic2013_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of carvedilol in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Carvedilol_Nikolic2013_reference</code></li><li><code>Carvedilol_Yamamoto2024_final</code></li><li><code>Carvedilol_Yamamoto2024_final_s_carvedilol_final_model_estim</code></li><li><code>Carvedilol_Hwang2023_PD_hr</code></li><li><code>Carvedilol_Yamamoto2024_PD_e</code></li></ul><h4>About carvedilol</h4><p>Carvedilol is a beta blocker with additional alpha-blocking activity used to treat high blood pressure, angina, heart failure, and other heart conditions such as after a myocardial infarction. It is an approved medicine and is widely used in cardiovascular care.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q412534\">Wikidata Q412534</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Carvedilol\">Carvedilol</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1123200, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Carvedilol;
